 and `claim_denied`, respectively. Strict dry-run is explicitly unsupported: it
 cannot claim to validate a future atomic close.
 
+For a retryable close, also send a stable `Idempotency-Key`. The receipt is
+looked up before checking a live lease, so an exact retry recovers the original
+close event even after its lease was released. The close-v2 fingerprint includes
+protocol, expected ClaimUID, client kind, and all legacy request inputs. Reusing
+a key with another tenure or downgrading to close-v1 returns
+`409 idempotency_mismatch`. Existing close-v1 receipt fingerprints are unchanged.
+An exact old receipt replay never closes a reopened issue or releases a new
+lease: it returns the original event and the current issue projection.
+
 The field is **optional in the schema** even though current daemons always send
 it. That is deliberate: a version-detection field has to survive version skew,
 so a client generated from a schema that includes it can still parse the
